      "## What Shopify actually costs",
      "Shopify is a hosted platform, which means you rent the shop, and Shopify runs the technology. The monthly plans are straightforward: Basic at $29 a month, Grow at $79 a month, and Advanced at $399 a month, with a cheaper rate if you pay yearly. Basic is enough for most small stores, and it includes hosting, security, a free SSL certificate, and a checkout that works, all of which WooCommerce owners must arrange separately. The cost that surprises new owners is the payment fee. If you use Shopify Payments, the card fee on the Basic plan is 2.9 percent plus 30 cents per order in the US, falling to 2.6 percent plus 30 cents on Grow and 2.4 percent plus 30 cents on Advanced. If you use a different payment provider instead, Shopify adds a further fee on top: 2 percent on Basic, 1 percent on Grow, and 0.6 percent on Advanced. That percentage is the largest cost in the whole comparison, and it grows with your sales. Then there are apps. Shopify includes the basics, but most stores add a few paid ones, reviews, email marketing, a loyalty programme, or better search, typically $20 to $60 a month in total. A premium theme is a one-off $100 to $500, and many stores start with a free theme and buy a better one later. For a small store on Basic with a few apps, the fixed cost is roughly $60 to $90 a month, before the percentage on every order.",
