      "An American small business owner searching for a new website faces the same problem as every other buyer: the quotes range from a few hundred dollars to fifty thousand and more, and nobody explains why. One freelancer says $2,500, an agency in New York says $25,000, a website builder says $29 a month, and all three claim to be building the same thing. They are not. The price of a website is decided by what it has to do, how well it has to do it, and who is accountable when it does not work. This guide gives American businesses an honest picture of website development cost in the USA in 2026: what freelancers and agencies actually charge, what the money buys, the hidden costs nobody puts in the quote, and how to compare prices fairly.",
      "## The short answer",
